WEBVTT

1
00:00:32,958 --> 00:00:35,208
CONDOLENCES, DATO' MEOR ABDUL
RAHMAN BIN DAENG UDA MOHD HASHIM

2
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:37,583
SUPREME GRANDMASTER OF SILAT
GAYONG MALAYSIA

3
00:00:37,666 --> 00:00:39,416
THIS FILM IS INSPIRED BY THE TRUE STORY
AND STRUGGLES OF THE LATE

4
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,208
DATO' MEOR ABDUL RAHMAN.
SOME OF THE EVENTS DEPICTED IN THIS FILM

5
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:43,375
ARE FICTIONAL AND DO NOT REPRESENT
ANY INDIVIDUALS OR ACTUAL EVENTS.

6
00:00:43,458 --> 00:00:45,500
ANY RESEMBLANCE IS COINCIDENTAL.

7
00:00:52,458 --> 00:00:56,083
INSPIRED BY A TRUE STORY

8
00:01:19,416 --> 00:01:21,791
IN 1945, JAPAN SURRENDERED.

9
00:01:28,916 --> 00:01:33,083
IN 1952, MEOR RETURNED TO SINGAPORE
AFTER BRITISH REOCCUPATION.

10
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:44,250
UNFORTUNATELY, SECRET SOCIETIES, GAMBLING,

11
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:45,750
PROSTITUTION, AND OPIUM ADDICTION
WERE WIDESPREAD.

12
00:01:55,125 --> 00:01:58,708
THE POLICE SQUAD
WENT THROUGH A DARK PERIOD

13
00:02:02,916 --> 00:02:05,291
DUE TO CORRUPTION

14
00:02:24,291 --> 00:02:25,458
Brother Mat.

15
00:02:26,208 --> 00:02:28,375
Hey! Where’s my money?!

16
00:02:28,458 --> 00:02:29,458
Hurry up!

17
00:02:31,916 --> 00:02:33,333
Hey! How dare you not to pay！

18
00:02:34,541 --> 00:02:36,166
Don’t you dare run away!

19
00:02:38,166 --> 00:02:39,666
Where are you trying to go?

20
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:41,583
Hey!

21
00:02:41,666 --> 00:02:44,333
My child is sick. I need money.

22
00:02:44,416 --> 00:02:46,125
Today, you’re sick.

23
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,083
Tomorrow, he’s sick.

24
00:02:48,166 --> 00:02:49,041
And the day after tomorrow, he is sick.

25
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:52,208
Everyone else has paid.

26
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:55,416
Do you think you’re special?

27
00:02:58,166 --> 00:03:00,000
Ah Keong, Sui Gu.

28
00:03:04,708 --> 00:03:05,916
Enough!

29
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:10,958
Who are you?

30
00:03:13,291 --> 00:03:14,708
Brother Mat.

31
00:03:14,791 --> 00:03:17,583
Oh, newcomer.

32
00:03:18,708 --> 00:03:19,583
Have you paid yet?

33
00:03:21,208 --> 00:03:22,708
Protection money!

34
00:03:23,916 --> 00:03:25,583
Don’t play a fool with me!

35
00:03:25,666 --> 00:03:26,500
Hurry up and pay!

36
00:03:27,458 --> 00:03:28,416
Don’t bother her.

37
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,083
If you bother her, I will call the police.

38
00:03:44,166 --> 00:03:45,416
Weakling!

39
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,958
Snacks!

40
00:05:53,041 --> 00:05:55,541
Cucur badak, ondeh-ondeh!

41
00:05:55,625 --> 00:05:57,625
Snacks!

42
00:05:57,708 --> 00:06:00,041
Cucur badak, ondeh-ondeh!

43
00:06:00,541 --> 00:06:02,666
-How much for one cucur badak?
-Five cents.

44
00:06:05,375 --> 00:06:06,208
{\an8}Thank you.

45
00:06:06,291 --> 00:06:08,583
{\an8}Snacks!

46
00:06:08,666 --> 00:06:11,000
Cucur badak, ondeh-ondeh!

47
00:06:29,458 --> 00:06:30,666
How did you know I was here?

48
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:32,000
That sound of your breathing, Mat.

49
00:06:32,083 --> 00:06:33,208
It sounds like a buffalo’s breathing.

50
00:06:33,291 --> 00:06:34,208
I can hear it from five miles away.

51
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:36,166
And even more so right behind the door.

52
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,916
A face like this,
and you still want to try again.

53
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:00,458
You’re too slow.

54
00:07:01,625 --> 00:07:02,625
Do it again.

55
00:07:14,875 --> 00:07:17,583
Too greedy.
Watch your words first. Do it again.

56
00:07:21,041 --> 00:07:22,833
Great! Continue!

57
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:40,708
Since when has a hole been here?

58
00:07:40,791 --> 00:07:42,125
Pay attention to your surroundings, Mat.

59
00:07:42,208 --> 00:07:43,875
Turn that into a strength.

60
00:07:43,958 --> 00:07:46,916
A good practitioner will always be
aware of their surroundings.

61
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,208
What's with that hole?

62
00:07:50,041 --> 00:07:51,125
Sister Chom put it there.

63
00:07:51,208 --> 00:07:53,041
She wants to make a vegetable garden.

64
00:07:53,125 --> 00:07:55,416
Fatimah! Good morning.

65
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:57,333
Good morning, Uncle.

66
00:07:58,208 --> 00:07:59,416
Have a safe journey.

67
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,625
Alright.

68
00:08:01,291 --> 00:08:03,458
Snacks!

69
00:08:42,833 --> 00:08:44,625
How come there’s no one inside?

70
00:08:45,958 --> 00:08:47,250
That's right, Teacher.

71
00:08:48,125 --> 00:08:50,750
How come there’s no one inside?

72
00:08:53,750 --> 00:08:55,750
The thugs I caught at the night market,

73
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:57,250
what happened to them?

74
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,541
What has happened to them, Teacher?

75
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,125
I don’t know either.

76
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:05,416
Hey, you!

77
00:09:07,333 --> 00:09:09,375
Did you see anyone inside the lockup?

78
00:09:09,458 --> 00:09:11,291
-No, sir.
-No?

79
00:09:11,375 --> 00:09:12,875
Don’t mess with me.

80
00:09:14,083 --> 00:09:15,625
Help me a bit.

81
00:09:18,541 --> 00:09:19,583
Teacher,

82
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:21,833
I am definitely sure.

83
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:23,791
No one has been inside that lockup

84
00:09:23,875 --> 00:09:25,583
since the start of the morning shift.

85
00:09:27,541 --> 00:09:28,833
And…

86
00:09:28,916 --> 00:09:29,875
and…

87
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:32,708
and I am definitely sure

88
00:09:32,791 --> 00:09:35,541
no one has come here, Teacher.

89
00:09:35,625 --> 00:09:36,916
Hurry up.

90
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,125
I am innocent, sir.

91
00:09:39,208 --> 00:09:40,708
Peter Malcolm?

92
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:46,958
Why should I have written it
if you were just going to say it out loud?

93
00:11:19,958 --> 00:11:21,208
{\an8}Oh, and Meor…

94
00:11:50,041 --> 00:11:52,166
He blacked out!

95
00:11:53,916 --> 00:11:55,000
He is knocked out.

96
00:11:55,083 --> 00:11:58,125
The undefeated winner is Peter Malcolm.

97
00:13:04,291 --> 00:13:05,166
Come on!

98
00:16:07,583 --> 00:16:08,833
Let me help you.

99
00:16:35,208 --> 00:16:36,291
What's that, Brother?

100
00:16:37,541 --> 00:16:38,625
Not sure.

101
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,041
When I pass my exam,

102
00:16:44,625 --> 00:16:45,916
I want to drive a truck like that too.

103
00:16:48,666 --> 00:16:49,541
Is Uncle Mat handsome?

104
00:16:52,666 --> 00:16:55,625
But what if Uncle Mat fails again?

105
00:16:55,708 --> 00:16:58,291
Hey, kid,
did you have too much sugar or what?

106
00:17:00,666 --> 00:17:01,666
SAKURA CLUB

107
00:17:53,125 --> 00:17:54,708
Hey, Malcolm.

108
00:18:14,416 --> 00:18:16,875
HU WEI TANG

109
00:19:57,750 --> 00:19:58,958
Thank you, Boss Khoon.

110
00:20:11,791 --> 00:20:12,708
Here.

111
00:20:23,875 --> 00:20:25,708
Just bear it.

112
00:20:25,791 --> 00:20:28,458
Grandma said if you apply it like this,

113
00:20:28,958 --> 00:20:30,791
the bruise marks will fade quickly.

114
00:20:35,916 --> 00:20:36,958
Mayang.

115
00:20:37,041 --> 00:20:37,875
Yes?

116
00:20:39,583 --> 00:20:41,500
If I pass the examination,

117
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:43,916
I can become a police officer.

118
00:20:44,958 --> 00:20:46,083
-Really?
-Yes.

119
00:20:47,541 --> 00:20:50,791
That means I will get a permanent job.

120
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:53,541
That’s good if that’s the case.

121
00:20:57,166 --> 00:20:58,625
After this…

122
00:21:03,291 --> 00:21:04,916
can you…

123
00:21:07,041 --> 00:21:07,875
What is it?

124
00:21:09,125 --> 00:21:10,625
Can you…

125
00:21:14,625 --> 00:21:17,625
Can you…

126
00:21:19,666 --> 00:21:21,083
Can you…

127
00:21:21,166 --> 00:21:24,125
-What it is?
-Will you share my happiness?

128
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,541
Of course, Brother Mat.

129
00:21:29,625 --> 00:21:32,208
My prayers are always
with you, Brother Mat.

130
00:21:34,750 --> 00:21:36,041
Why is it so hard to say?

131
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:38,166
-Miss.
-Yes?

132
00:21:38,750 --> 00:21:40,208
Have you already closed your stall?

133
00:21:40,291 --> 00:21:41,416
Not yet.

134
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,541
Can I have one cendol?

135
00:21:42,625 --> 00:21:43,750
Sure. Please wait a moment.

136
00:21:45,083 --> 00:21:46,083
Here!

137
00:21:49,125 --> 00:21:50,500
Which type of cendol do you want?

138
00:21:50,583 --> 00:21:52,250
As usual. With extra peanuts.

139
00:21:52,333 --> 00:21:53,541
Extra peanuts.

140
00:21:58,416 --> 00:21:59,625
Is that even possible?

141
00:21:59,708 --> 00:22:02,625
The doctor said I’m overweight.

142
00:22:02,708 --> 00:22:05,750
This isn’t being overweight,
it’s happiness.

143
00:22:05,833 --> 00:22:07,375
Happiness.

144
00:22:07,458 --> 00:22:11,208
Listen to the doctor
and eat less oily food.

145
00:22:12,875 --> 00:22:14,166
Who are you?

146
00:22:21,208 --> 00:22:23,500
-Fauzi.
-Fauzi?

147
00:22:23,583 --> 00:22:24,750
Good morning, everyone.

148
00:22:24,833 --> 00:22:27,250
-Good morning, Teacher.
-Good morning, Teacher.

149
00:22:27,333 --> 00:22:28,416
Fauzi, you are here.

150
00:22:29,333 --> 00:22:30,458
Meor.

151
00:22:38,208 --> 00:22:39,583
No need to be too formal.

152
00:22:40,083 --> 00:22:42,208
Friends, this is Fauzi,
my partner starting today.

153
00:22:43,250 --> 00:22:44,541
-Teacher.
-What?

154
00:22:44,625 --> 00:22:46,041
Teacher, do you remember
this person, Worawut?

155
00:22:46,125 --> 00:22:47,458
Worawut?

156
00:22:47,541 --> 00:22:48,708
That Muay Thai fighter?

157
00:22:53,041 --> 00:22:54,458
What’s wrong with this Thai guy?

158
00:22:54,541 --> 00:22:55,958
Looking for trouble all around the world?

159
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:57,875
Who is he? Wuro what？

160
00:22:58,458 --> 00:22:59,250
Worawut.

161
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:00,708
Listen to what I’m about to tell you.

162
00:23:00,791 --> 00:23:03,166
Can you believe that arrogant Worawut

163
00:23:03,250 --> 00:23:05,750
got beaten up by our Panglima Sendo Perak?

164
00:23:05,833 --> 00:23:07,833
Panglima Sendo of Perak？

165
00:23:07,916 --> 00:23:08,958
Hey!

166
00:23:09,041 --> 00:23:10,083
There.

167
00:23:12,083 --> 00:23:14,750
That was the best fight I’ve ever seen.

168
00:23:15,666 --> 00:23:16,500
Rizal, come show us.

169
00:23:19,833 --> 00:23:20,833
Wrong person.

170
00:23:24,375 --> 00:23:25,458
Ali.

171
00:23:25,541 --> 00:23:30,583
Fight!

172
00:23:30,666 --> 00:23:32,166
This is how he fought back.

173
00:23:34,625 --> 00:23:36,625
Ali, you be Worawut.

174
00:23:36,708 --> 00:23:37,958
-Who?
-Worawut.

175
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:38,916
Oh, Worawut.

176
00:23:41,583 --> 00:23:43,375
-Take it slow, Ali.
-Alright.

177
00:23:44,041 --> 00:23:45,208
-Teacher blocked.
-What did Teacher do after that?

178
00:23:45,291 --> 00:23:46,166
-Catch him.
-What happened next?

179
00:23:46,250 --> 00:23:47,583
-Teacher caught him like this.
-Then?

180
00:23:47,666 --> 00:23:49,708
-Then Teacher did this.
-Ouch!

181
00:23:51,458 --> 00:23:53,041
Was it like this, Teacher?

182
00:23:53,125 --> 00:23:55,541
It wasn't that dramatic,
not to that extent.

183
00:23:57,500 --> 00:23:58,666
Thank you, Ali.

184
00:23:59,291 --> 00:24:00,291
Teacher,

185
00:24:01,250 --> 00:24:03,666
if I were you,

186
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:07,291
I’d beat him until even his parents
didn't recognize him.

187
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:12,416
Why bother hitting
an opponent who is already down?

188
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:14,750
That will only prevent him
from receiving the lesson

189
00:24:14,833 --> 00:24:16,125
that God has prepared for him.

190
00:24:16,208 --> 00:24:17,500
Teacher,

191
00:24:17,583 --> 00:24:20,625
is it true that all silat grandmasters
are invulnerable?

192
00:24:20,708 --> 00:24:22,375
Nonsense. Bullshit.

193
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,666
We shouldn’t believe things like that.

194
00:24:29,250 --> 00:24:30,708
It’s already 1950.

195
00:24:31,958 --> 00:24:33,041
We're in the modern age,

196
00:24:34,166 --> 00:24:36,541
the era of science and industry.

197
00:24:42,833 --> 00:24:43,833
If your child is sick,

198
00:24:45,375 --> 00:24:48,083
would you take him to the hospital
or to a traditional healer?

199
00:24:50,458 --> 00:24:52,125
We are all civil servants.

200
00:24:53,875 --> 00:24:57,166
How can we believe
in mumbo jumbo stuff like that?

201
00:24:57,250 --> 00:24:58,583
Hey, newbie,

202
00:24:59,083 --> 00:25:00,541
it’s not good to speak like that.

203
00:25:00,625 --> 00:25:03,416
I’m here to work,

204
00:25:03,916 --> 00:25:05,083
not to socialize.

205
00:25:05,750 --> 00:25:06,833
Don’t you have any manners?

206
00:25:07,583 --> 00:25:08,666
Manners?

207
00:25:08,750 --> 00:25:10,708
Manners won’t get our work done.

208
00:25:15,416 --> 00:25:16,583
This.

209
00:25:16,666 --> 00:25:18,666
This is what gets our work done.

210
00:25:20,916 --> 00:25:23,541
All that fuss earlier

211
00:25:23,625 --> 00:25:25,666
doesn't stand a chance against this.

212
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:32,833
Never point that at your own people.

213
00:25:36,083 --> 00:25:37,583
There’s not even a bullet in there.

214
00:25:37,666 --> 00:25:39,250
Of course there isn’t. If there had been,

215
00:25:39,333 --> 00:25:40,208
my head would've been blown off.

216
00:25:40,291 --> 00:25:41,500
Hey, kid.

217
00:25:41,583 --> 00:25:43,375
You still have a lot to learn.

218
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:45,041
Listen to me.

219
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:47,708
Even a pistol isn’t the fastest weapon.

220
00:25:47,791 --> 00:25:50,041
Learn from who? From you?

221
00:25:50,125 --> 00:25:52,250
At least I still can see

222
00:25:52,333 --> 00:25:53,791
my own feet when I bend down.

223
00:25:54,291 --> 00:25:55,583
What Pak Man said is true.

224
00:25:55,666 --> 00:25:57,875
A pistol isn’t always faster.

225
00:25:57,958 --> 00:25:58,791
Bullshit.

226
00:25:58,875 --> 00:26:01,833
You were just lucky earlier
because I wasn’t ready.

227
00:26:03,833 --> 00:26:04,750
What about this?

228
00:26:06,166 --> 00:26:08,416
If you can prove that he’s right,

229
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,000
I will apologize to him.

230
00:26:11,416 --> 00:26:12,916
-Teacher, there’s no need.
-It’s okay, Pak Man.

231
00:26:55,041 --> 00:26:57,000
Thank you for being willing
to train with me.

232
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:07,541
Teacher!

233
00:27:09,458 --> 00:27:10,625
Such power, Teacher!

234
00:27:13,166 --> 00:27:14,125
"Bullshit."

235
00:27:50,250 --> 00:27:52,708
Keep it. I don’t smoke.

236
00:28:01,875 --> 00:28:03,083
Don’t take too long.

237
00:28:04,500 --> 00:28:06,583
We still have a lot of work
that needs to be done.

238
00:28:32,416 --> 00:28:33,958
I want to find all the cases that

239
00:28:34,041 --> 00:28:36,416
Peter Malcolm closed three years ago.

240
00:28:37,833 --> 00:28:38,833
What?

241
00:28:42,416 --> 00:28:44,041
Many of these files don't have labels.

242
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:47,416
In that case,
we’d better start right away.

243
00:30:27,125 --> 00:30:29,666
Today, there’s been progress in the case.

244
00:30:30,166 --> 00:30:32,291
If I keep going,

245
00:30:33,208 --> 00:30:35,333
I will definitely find the truth.

246
00:30:37,583 --> 00:30:39,875
I don’t know how far this thing goes

247
00:30:41,375 --> 00:30:43,333
or how many people are involved.

248
00:30:46,333 --> 00:30:48,458
Should I continue?

249
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:52,750
Are you worried
that others might be affected?

250
00:31:11,666 --> 00:31:13,125
That's it?

251
00:31:14,083 --> 00:31:16,083
I thought it was
something really serious just now.

252
00:31:16,791 --> 00:31:18,166
This is serious, Chom.

253
00:31:19,041 --> 00:31:21,625
Dear, do you remember

254
00:31:22,708 --> 00:31:24,541
what you told me

255
00:31:25,125 --> 00:31:27,166
before you took this police job?

256
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:29,875
You said

257
00:31:30,916 --> 00:31:32,625
you wanted to do the right thing.

258
00:31:33,666 --> 00:31:35,083
For God,

259
00:31:36,166 --> 00:31:37,500
for yourself,

260
00:31:38,375 --> 00:31:39,833
for your family,

261
00:31:41,375 --> 00:31:42,666
and for the people.

262
00:31:45,791 --> 00:31:46,958
So right now,

263
00:31:48,583 --> 00:31:50,958
are you still doing the right thing?

264
00:31:55,083 --> 00:31:56,000
There.

265
00:31:57,125 --> 00:31:59,000
That’s the answer.

266
00:32:03,166 --> 00:32:04,375
Do not doubt.

267
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:07,625
Do not be afraid.

268
00:32:08,375 --> 00:32:09,750
God says,

269
00:32:11,083 --> 00:32:12,708
"Do not fear,

270
00:32:13,708 --> 00:32:16,083
for I am with you."

271
00:32:19,250 --> 00:32:22,750
"I hear and see everything."

272
00:32:31,291 --> 00:32:32,500
Mat.

273
00:32:33,666 --> 00:32:34,916
Can I ask for your help?

274
00:32:39,416 --> 00:32:41,250
I'm currently investigating a case,

275
00:32:42,875 --> 00:32:44,416
and I'll be quite busy.

276
00:32:45,416 --> 00:32:48,458
I might be spending
a lot of time at the station,

277
00:32:49,416 --> 00:32:50,750
so I want to ask for your help

278
00:32:50,833 --> 00:32:53,291
to look after Sister Chom
and the kids at home.

279
00:32:56,250 --> 00:32:57,500
Of course.

280
00:32:57,583 --> 00:32:59,541
You can count on me.

281
00:33:00,250 --> 00:33:01,750
Just leave everything to me.

282
00:33:08,541 --> 00:33:09,708
Thank you, Mat.

283
00:33:21,875 --> 00:33:24,458
<i>We know that Malcolm accepted bribes,</i>

284
00:33:24,541 --> 00:33:26,291
<i>but it's not clear from whom.</i>

285
00:33:26,875 --> 00:33:31,583
<i>We’ll investigate all his cases</i>
<i>from the past three years.</i>

286
00:33:31,666 --> 00:33:35,416
<i>We’ll check and cross-reference</i>
<i>with those who were arrested.</i>

287
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:45,250
IDENTIFIED

288
00:33:45,333 --> 00:33:48,875
The Sungai Gang had
a total of 128 arrests.

289
00:33:48,958 --> 00:33:51,500
The Tiger Clan had a total of 24 arrests.

290
00:33:53,416 --> 00:33:54,583
Twenty-four?

291
00:33:54,666 --> 00:33:56,791
In a period of three years,

292
00:33:56,875 --> 00:33:59,791
out of a total of 384 arrests,

293
00:34:01,166 --> 00:34:02,666
they only had 24?

294
00:34:13,708 --> 00:34:16,041
<i>If Malcolm's working with Lee Khoon,</i>

295
00:34:16,125 --> 00:34:19,500
<i>he must protect these places from raids.</i>

296
00:34:20,041 --> 00:34:22,416
<i>Next, we just need to identify</i>

297
00:34:22,500 --> 00:34:24,666
<i>which places belong to the Tiger Clan</i>

298
00:34:24,750 --> 00:34:27,250
<i>by following the people from Lee Khoon</i>

299
00:34:27,333 --> 00:34:29,416
<i>who collect protection money.</i>

300
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:36,500
PROSPERITY

301
00:34:41,500 --> 00:34:43,916
Hey! You still haven't paid?
Watch out. I'll beat you up!

302
00:34:48,041 --> 00:34:49,791
<i>After we identify them,</i>

303
00:34:49,875 --> 00:34:51,833
<i>we will raid those places.</i>

304
00:34:51,916 --> 00:34:53,583
<i>Malcolm must have something.</i>

305
00:34:54,541 --> 00:34:56,125
<i>We’ll use the opportunity</i>
<i>to gather evidence</i>

306
00:34:56,208 --> 00:34:58,250
<i>that Malcolm and Lee Khoon</i>
<i>are working together.</i>

307
00:36:15,958 --> 00:36:18,041
He still hasn’t left with the bag.

308
00:36:19,625 --> 00:36:20,500
This is weird.

309
00:36:23,125 --> 00:36:24,208
So what should we do?

310
00:36:25,041 --> 00:36:27,166
Do we need to include
this place in the list too?

311
00:36:31,250 --> 00:36:32,583
What is this place?

312
00:36:35,041 --> 00:36:36,375
I want to go take a look.

313
00:36:38,875 --> 00:36:39,791
I will follow you.

314
00:36:42,375 --> 00:36:43,541
No.

315
00:36:44,333 --> 00:36:45,166
Why?

316
00:36:46,208 --> 00:36:47,125
Not suitable.

317
00:36:49,541 --> 00:36:51,250
I’ll go in for a moment. You wait here.

318
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:04,875
Sir.

319
00:38:06,041 --> 00:38:07,000
What are you doing here?

320
00:38:16,625 --> 00:38:17,625
What happened?

321
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,208
Hey, why are you taking off your clothes?

322
00:38:21,208 --> 00:38:22,041
Oh, great.

323
00:38:23,625 --> 00:38:25,083
Say it. Tell me, what's happening?

324
00:39:08,916 --> 00:39:09,833
Hey!

325
00:39:13,458 --> 00:39:14,958
Do you know who I am?

326
00:39:16,708 --> 00:39:17,625
What are you going to do to me?

327
00:39:19,125 --> 00:39:20,541
All of you better remember

328
00:39:21,208 --> 00:39:23,500
you’ll be in big trouble

329
00:39:24,083 --> 00:39:25,833
if anything happens to me.

330
00:39:27,875 --> 00:39:29,750
-Understand?
-Who are you?

331
00:39:30,541 --> 00:39:31,541
You are a dead man.

332
00:39:32,875 --> 00:39:34,333
But don’t be afraid.

333
00:39:34,416 --> 00:39:36,000
This is my boss’s place.

334
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:40,041
No one will know you died here!

335
00:39:42,375 --> 00:39:43,500
Hey!

336
00:39:49,458 --> 00:39:51,833
Whoever kills him first

337
00:39:52,541 --> 00:39:55,708
will gets triple the money from me!

338
00:39:55,791 --> 00:39:57,083
Kill him!

339
00:40:07,875 --> 00:40:08,833
Fauzi,

340
00:40:09,583 --> 00:40:10,791
get out of here now.

341
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,833
Yeah!

342
00:41:37,625 --> 00:41:39,083
<i>I want to say thank you</i>

343
00:41:40,625 --> 00:41:42,333
for saving me at that place.

344
00:41:44,833 --> 00:41:47,041
You would’ve done the same for me.

345
00:41:48,916 --> 00:41:49,916
No.

346
00:41:50,916 --> 00:41:53,125
I don’t think I would’ve done
the same, because…

347
00:41:54,833 --> 00:41:57,291
-I don’t have your…
-"Mumbo Jumbo?"

348
00:42:03,541 --> 00:42:04,833
Skills.

349
00:42:06,750 --> 00:42:08,625
And I should apologize

350
00:42:09,541 --> 00:42:11,458
for what I said earlier about silat.

351
00:42:13,166 --> 00:42:14,166
Fauzi.

352
00:42:14,666 --> 00:42:17,750
I'm not affected

353
00:42:18,958 --> 00:42:20,500
by what you said.

354
00:42:22,083 --> 00:42:23,666
But some of our friends

355
00:42:25,083 --> 00:42:26,500
were hurt by it.

356
00:42:32,416 --> 00:42:33,500
Understood.

357
00:42:34,916 --> 00:42:37,000
I will apologize to Pak Man and Rizal.

358
00:42:40,541 --> 00:42:42,750
Actually, there’s one
more thing I want to say.

359
00:42:48,708 --> 00:42:50,791
Is it okay if I call you "teacher" too?

360
00:42:51,500 --> 00:42:52,916
And learn silat from you?

361
00:43:00,666 --> 00:43:02,625
You’re a graduate
with a scholarship, right?

362
00:43:03,416 --> 00:43:04,250
Yes.

363
00:43:11,166 --> 00:43:12,958
There's fish, pineapple.

364
00:43:13,041 --> 00:43:14,291
-Brother.
-Yes?

365
00:43:14,375 --> 00:43:16,666
-Where is the cendol shop?
-Over there.

366
00:43:16,750 --> 00:43:18,250
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

367
00:43:25,875 --> 00:43:27,041
-Mayang.
-Yes?

368
00:43:29,375 --> 00:43:30,666
My name is Fauzi.

369
00:43:30,750 --> 00:43:32,083
Brother Meor sent me.

370
00:43:32,166 --> 00:43:33,166
Where's Mat?

371
00:43:33,791 --> 00:43:35,250
You are Brother Mat's friend?

372
00:43:35,333 --> 00:43:37,000
Brother Mat will be here in a moment.

373
00:43:37,083 --> 00:43:38,125
Please have a seat first.

374
00:43:38,208 --> 00:43:40,208
-Do you want cendol?
-It's okay.

375
00:43:40,291 --> 00:43:42,666
-No need to trouble you.
-No worries.

376
00:43:42,750 --> 00:43:44,166
-Brother Mat’s friend is my friend too.
-Ah.

377
00:43:45,750 --> 00:43:46,916
No worries. Please have a seat first.

378
00:44:04,291 --> 00:44:05,500
Brother Fauzi.

379
00:44:10,416 --> 00:44:11,958
-I'm sorry.
-It's okay.

380
00:44:12,041 --> 00:44:13,250
I didn’t mean to.

381
00:44:13,333 --> 00:44:14,583
-Hey!
-Brother Mat!

382
00:44:18,125 --> 00:44:19,125
Fake Malay!

383
00:44:20,375 --> 00:44:21,625
Brother Mat!

384
00:44:23,333 --> 00:44:24,708
Brother Fauzi!

385
00:44:24,791 --> 00:44:26,333
-Please don’t fight!
-What's wrong with you?

386
00:44:35,250 --> 00:44:36,416
What's wrong with you?

387
00:44:47,833 --> 00:44:50,000
Didn't I already tell you
not to fight, Brother Mat?

388
00:44:54,416 --> 00:44:55,791
Serves you right!

389
00:44:56,458 --> 00:44:57,625
Here.

390
00:44:57,708 --> 00:44:58,833
Twenty cents.

391
00:45:01,208 --> 00:45:02,333
Why is it so expensive?

392
00:45:02,416 --> 00:45:04,583
This vegetable was imported
from the Cameron Highlands.

393
00:45:20,875 --> 00:45:21,875
You were saying that

394
00:45:22,375 --> 00:45:23,291
Brother Meor asked you to come?

395
00:45:24,791 --> 00:45:25,875
Yes.

396
00:45:26,500 --> 00:45:28,083
I’m here to help you pass the examination.

397
00:45:28,166 --> 00:45:29,166
So?

398
00:45:30,250 --> 00:45:31,416
Why were you holding Mayang's hand?

399
00:45:33,000 --> 00:45:34,958
When did I hold her hand?

400
00:45:35,041 --> 00:45:38,125
The cendol fell. I was holding
the bowl, not her hand.

401
00:45:42,958 --> 00:45:44,000
Fake Malay,

402
00:45:44,083 --> 00:45:45,166
I'm sorry.

403
00:45:45,250 --> 00:45:46,875
I really need to pass this exam.

404
00:45:46,958 --> 00:45:48,250
Please help me.

405
00:45:49,625 --> 00:45:52,000
Oh, my, what has
Teacher Meor gotten me into?

406
00:45:55,500 --> 00:45:56,708
Continue.

407
00:46:03,458 --> 00:46:05,166
-Ah, Chai!
-Yes, Teacher.

408
00:46:05,666 --> 00:46:06,875
Keep your stances lower.

409
00:46:06,958 --> 00:46:08,125
Alright, Teacher.

410
00:46:10,250 --> 00:46:11,125
Continue.

411
00:46:16,291 --> 00:46:18,000
So tired.

412
00:46:33,375 --> 00:46:35,166
Time to learn!

413
00:46:36,458 --> 00:46:37,791
Ugh,

414
00:46:37,875 --> 00:46:41,208
let me rest for a day. Just a day.
We can continue tomorrow.

415
00:46:41,291 --> 00:46:43,833
Tomorrow?
So you don’t want to pass, right?

416
00:46:48,500 --> 00:46:50,625
Come on. What are you waiting for?

417
00:46:50,708 --> 00:46:51,625
Do you want me to pass or not?

418
00:46:53,166 --> 00:46:56,291
-You!
-Watch my head. You'll mess up my brain.

419
00:46:56,375 --> 00:46:57,666
Since when do you have a brain?

420
00:47:18,750 --> 00:47:19,875
Do you want to teach or not?

421
00:47:37,750 --> 00:47:38,583
I'll be right back.

422
00:48:57,958 --> 00:49:00,291
Thank you, Brother Mat,
for taking me home.

423
00:49:00,958 --> 00:49:02,500
You are welcome.

424
00:49:02,583 --> 00:49:04,791
I won’t let you go home alone.

425
00:49:12,708 --> 00:49:15,791
Brother Mat, if you pass your exam later,

426
00:49:15,875 --> 00:49:17,333
I want to buy you a gift.

427
00:49:18,291 --> 00:49:19,375
No need.

428
00:49:19,458 --> 00:49:20,625
Keep that money.

429
00:49:20,708 --> 00:49:22,416
Leave it. It's my money.

430
00:49:47,083 --> 00:49:48,458
Brother!

431
00:49:55,625 --> 00:49:57,666
Brother! I managed
to answer all the questions!

432
00:49:57,750 --> 00:49:59,375
My mind didn’t go blank this time.

433
00:49:59,458 --> 00:50:00,833
Fauzi!

434
00:50:00,916 --> 00:50:02,625
Thank you!

435
00:50:06,791 --> 00:50:07,750
Listen.

436
00:50:07,833 --> 00:50:10,583
Your hard work paid off. Praise be to God.

437
00:50:10,666 --> 00:50:13,416
Hopefully, before long,
we can become colleagues!

438
00:50:17,291 --> 00:50:19,125
I want to tell Mayang! I’m going now!

439
00:50:20,791 --> 00:50:22,250
Don’t forget tomorrow!

440
00:50:22,333 --> 00:50:25,166
Sister Chom has invited
everyone for dinner.

441
00:50:25,250 --> 00:50:26,250
Alright!

442
00:50:37,958 --> 00:50:39,250
There’s a ship with a suspicious weight

443
00:50:39,333 --> 00:50:41,500
coming from Hong Kong.

444
00:50:42,125 --> 00:50:44,833
It’s registered under the name Lee Geok.

445
00:50:44,916 --> 00:50:46,791
Lee Geok?
That’s Lee Khoon’s adopted child.

446
00:50:47,625 --> 00:50:48,625
Jade.

447
00:50:50,166 --> 00:50:51,500
It’s scheduled to arrive tonight.

448
00:51:32,208 --> 00:51:34,750
If Lee Khoon’s adopted child is here,

449
00:51:36,291 --> 00:51:38,375
the item must be important.

450
00:51:39,375 --> 00:51:42,500
Do you think those items
are what we think they are?

451
00:51:46,666 --> 00:51:49,000
There’s only one way to be sure.

452
00:51:54,583 --> 00:51:55,500
<i>Alright. Listen up, everyone.</i>

453
00:51:57,583 --> 00:52:00,250
This is an emergency operation.

454
00:52:00,791 --> 00:52:04,208
We will move straight
to the warehouse to carry out a raid.

455
00:52:04,708 --> 00:52:06,208
If you encounter anyone, I repeat,

456
00:52:06,291 --> 00:52:08,625
if you encounter anyone
who doesn’t cooperate,

457
00:52:08,708 --> 00:52:10,333
just detain them.

458
00:52:13,708 --> 00:52:15,250
-Police!
-Freeze!

459
00:52:19,625 --> 00:52:20,833
Don't move!

460
00:52:22,875 --> 00:52:24,000
This is a search warrant.

461
00:52:25,291 --> 00:52:26,875
You are all required to cooperate.

462
00:52:27,625 --> 00:52:29,916
Anyone who resists will be arrested!

463
00:54:19,750 --> 00:54:20,583
Teacher.

464
00:54:21,583 --> 00:54:23,291
Wait a moment, Teacher, I’ll keep looking.

465
00:54:26,291 --> 00:54:27,375
There’s more, Teacher!

466
00:54:28,041 --> 00:54:30,041
There’s really a lot of opium here.

467
00:54:30,833 --> 00:54:31,958
Enough to fill an entire truck!

468
00:54:36,916 --> 00:54:37,791
Boss Khoon!

469
00:54:38,666 --> 00:54:39,541
What happened?

470
00:54:39,625 --> 00:54:42,541
Boss Khoon, our warehouse!
It’s been raided by the police!

471
00:54:45,416 --> 00:54:46,250
What about the goods?

472
00:54:46,333 --> 00:54:48,000
They were all seized by the police!

473
00:54:58,458 --> 00:55:00,458
-Where’s Geok?
-Arrested by the police.

474
00:55:05,916 --> 00:55:07,958
Tell Malcolm to come to see me.

475
00:55:17,416 --> 00:55:18,791
Attention!

476
00:56:52,083 --> 00:56:56,750
HU WEI TANG

477
00:58:05,541 --> 00:58:08,375
-Put this in living room, please.
-Alright, Sister Chom.

478
00:58:08,458 --> 00:58:09,708
Aishah.

479
00:58:09,791 --> 00:58:12,083
Aishah, it’s Cik Mat's turn.

480
00:58:22,916 --> 00:58:24,791
-Mat.
-Yes?

481
00:58:24,875 --> 00:58:25,875
Come here.

482
00:58:29,333 --> 00:58:31,125
-You all go ahead and play first.
-Okay.

483
00:58:32,791 --> 00:58:34,875
-Sister Mayang, come play with us.
-Okay.

484
00:58:38,166 --> 00:58:39,666
That's far.

485
00:58:40,583 --> 00:58:42,708
-You ready?
-Yes.

486
00:59:41,125 --> 00:59:42,041
Mat!

487
01:00:00,333 --> 01:00:01,541
Sister Chom!

488
01:00:03,083 --> 01:00:04,333
Mayang!

489
01:00:04,416 --> 01:00:06,166
Save the children!

490
01:00:12,500 --> 01:00:13,458
Mat!

491
01:00:15,041 --> 01:00:15,833
Mat!

492
01:00:21,583 --> 01:00:22,791
Mat!

493
01:00:22,875 --> 01:00:24,875
-Sister Chom!
-Mom!

494
01:00:24,958 --> 01:00:26,500
Kak Chom!

495
01:00:31,833 --> 01:00:33,083
Mat!

496
01:00:34,458 --> 01:00:36,833
Mom!

497
01:00:36,916 --> 01:00:39,250
Let us go! Let go! Mom!

498
01:00:47,250 --> 01:00:48,583
Mat!

499
01:00:51,291 --> 01:00:52,291
Mom!

500
01:01:04,625 --> 01:01:05,583
Mom!

501
01:01:08,500 --> 01:01:09,666
Mom!

502
01:01:15,458 --> 01:01:17,666
<i>I want to ask you to please look after</i>

503
01:01:17,750 --> 01:01:19,375
<i>Sister Chom and the kids at home.</i>

504
01:01:20,208 --> 01:01:21,541
<i>Of course.</i>

505
01:01:22,125 --> 01:01:23,250
You can count on me.

506
01:01:23,333 --> 01:01:24,375
Just leave everything to me.

507
01:01:25,625 --> 01:01:26,916
<i>Thank you, Mat.</i>

508
01:01:49,375 --> 01:01:50,458
Mat!

509
01:01:51,208 --> 01:01:52,500
Mat!

510
01:01:57,125 --> 01:01:58,416
Sister Mayang!

511
01:02:08,541 --> 01:02:09,625
Fauzi.

512
01:02:09,708 --> 01:02:11,166
There’s a celebration for Mat tonight.

513
01:02:11,250 --> 01:02:13,416
-Let’s go back early.
-Sure.

514
01:02:14,500 --> 01:02:15,791
We’re heading out first, guys.

515
01:02:16,291 --> 01:02:17,333
Goodbye, Teacher.

516
01:02:22,250 --> 01:02:24,416
Let go of my children!

517
01:02:24,500 --> 01:02:26,083
Let go!

518
01:02:27,541 --> 01:02:28,666
Mom!

519
01:02:29,791 --> 01:02:31,416
Let us go!

520
01:02:34,000 --> 01:02:35,666
Mat!

521
01:02:39,833 --> 01:02:41,875
Cik Mat!

522
01:02:42,791 --> 01:02:44,916
Sister Mayang.

523
01:02:48,125 --> 01:02:49,083
Cik Mat!

524
01:02:50,375 --> 01:02:51,833
Sister Mayang.

525
01:03:20,291 --> 01:03:22,083
Kak Mayang.

526
01:03:26,958 --> 01:03:28,000
Come quickly!

527
01:03:31,333 --> 01:03:32,750
How pitiful.

528
01:03:32,833 --> 01:03:33,875
What happened?

529
01:03:35,791 --> 01:03:36,750
Hurry!

530
01:04:49,500 --> 01:04:55,125
I’m sorry…

531
01:05:00,875 --> 01:05:03,208
I’ve disappointed you.

532
01:05:08,666 --> 01:05:10,875
You did your best.

533
01:05:12,791 --> 01:05:14,541
I’m proud of you.

534
01:05:44,291 --> 01:05:45,458
I understand.

535
01:05:48,875 --> 01:05:50,083
I understand.

536
01:05:55,958 --> 01:05:57,916
Repeat what I say.

537
01:05:58,708 --> 01:05:59,750
Okay?

538
01:06:01,083 --> 01:06:05,583
I bear witness
that there is no god but Allah.

539
01:06:05,666 --> 01:06:06,708
Repeat after me.

540
01:06:08,458 --> 01:06:14,958
I bear witness
that there is no god but Allah.

541
01:06:16,875 --> 01:06:23,000
And I bear witness
that Muhammad is the messenger of Allah.

542
01:06:24,291 --> 01:06:26,208
<i>And I bear witness</i>

543
01:06:26,291 --> 01:06:32,416
<i>that Muhammad is the messenger of Allah.</i>

544
01:06:37,500 --> 01:06:39,125
